# Project Context

This project studies motor imagery EEG decoding on the Shanghai University WBCIC-SHU 2C dataset.

**Current mainline = cross-session domain generalization (DG):** measure and reduce the accuracy
drop when training on one session and testing on another session of the SAME subject. Stages:
(A) drift diagnostics → (B) static baselines (EEGNet/DeepConvNet/FBCNet) at within-session CV +
single-source cross-session → (Step 1) multi-source `ses-01+02 → ses-03` → (Step 2, DONE)
no-learning / unsupervised alignment baseline → (Step 3, future) learning-based / online adaptation.

Long-term vision (NOT the current runnable mainline): a **Confidence-aware Online Adaptive
Multi-Subagent Pretraining Framework** (full CAP-EEGNet) + the 41/10 cross-subject pretrain →
fine-tune → online plan. Kept in `docs/ROADMAP.md`; CAP-EEGNet exists only as a v1 skeleton
(encoder + classifier + confidence head; the rest raises `NotImplementedError`). The authoritative,
up-to-date status is always `docs/PROJECT_STATUS_CURRENT.md` — read it first if this rule and the
docs ever disagree.

Dataset:
- Use the 2C dataset first.
- 51 subjects.
- 3 sessions per subject.
- 2 classes: left-hand grasping MI and right-hand grasping MI.
- Each session has 200 trials, 100 per class.
- Raw data are stored outside this project directory.
- Raw files are data.bdf and evt.bdf.
- Final processed shape per session must be [trials, channels, time] = [200, 58, 1000].

Models (current mainline):
- EEGNet (Lawhern 2018) / DeepConvNet (Schirrmeister 2017) / FBCNet (Mane 2021), plus CAP-EEGNet
  v1 (skeleton). All share a `{logits, features, confidence}` forward contract + one trainer +
  one metric set so comparisons are fair. Build via `src/models/registry.build_model`.

Critical constraints:
- Split by subject/session, NEVER by trial. The early-stopping val slice is carved ONLY from train.
- For cross-session / multi-source / adaptation: the TEST session's labels are NEVER used for
  train / validation / early-stopping / tuning / method-selection. Only the test X (unlabeled) may
  be used for test-time statistics; `y_test` is for final evaluation only.
- No `optimizer.step` on the target except BatchNorm running-stat refresh (the BN-adaptation method).
- Online learning (future) must be test-then-update.
- Do not hard-code dataset paths (use `configs/paths.yaml`).
- Reference / handoff folders the senior shares are READ-ONLY: read + integrate sensibly into this
  repo's `src`/`scripts`/`configs`/`docs`; never run from them or copy draft code verbatim. No
  specific folder path is a permanent instruction — act only when the user points you at one.

Implementation language:
- All main pipelines (preprocessing, training, cross-subject, fine-tuning, online) MUST be Python/PyTorch.
- The dataset authors' MATLAB script (preprocessed.m) and the Neuracle toolbox are a
  REFERENCE RECIPE ONLY. They must NOT be a runtime dependency.
- The paper-processed `.mat` files in `derivatives/` may be used as an event/label
  ground-truth CROSS-CHECK, but are NOT the main training data entry point.

